cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Science-Skill in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Science-Skill: Claude Code skills against the failure modes of AI-assisted research"
authors:
  - alias: OIerYangJZ
repository-code: "https://github.com/OIerYangJZ/Science-Skill"
url: "https://github.com/OIerYangJZ/Science-Skill"
abstract: >-
  A library of Claude Code skills that counter recurring failure modes of
  AI-assisted research: defensive or inflated writing, numbers that drift from
  the data, code that does not implement the described design, unchecked proof
  steps, fabricated or misattributed references, self-confirming novelty
  searches, venue choices made from memory, mock reviews that are not
  independent, and optimistic progress reports. Each skill is a written
  procedure backed by standard-library Python scripts that measure, trace or
  verify.
keywords:
  - research integrity
  - scientific writing
  - reproducibility
  - peer review
  - Claude Code
  - agent skills
license: MIT
version: 0.4.0
date-released: "2026-10-29"
